##general idea (for ancappers)
###Lessons Learned: Problems in Education
##isolated individuals/families: on-going, many nodes (robinson curriculum)
##cooperative groups: common home-schooling?
##christian v. non-christian
##education v. training (see [http://www.sourcetext.com/grammarian/ Richard Mitchell], The Underground Grammarian)
##classical v. standard (see [http://www.sourcetext.com/grammarian/ Richard Mitchell], again)

The systemic effects on children of mass schooling is deadly to the brain.

Coop groups have to be informed, not to institute alternative mass schooling, but to support homeschooling.

&nbsp;

As an example, note Heather, unschooled after 2nd grade, and at 17 built her own [http://www.homestead.com/peaceandcarrots/HeathersHouse.html house] and rebuilt her [http://www.heathershikinghiatus.com/FixingUpVan.html old van] and ... and ...





